From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anvill <anvill@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:37:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Sleigh-based SPARC64; fix Sleigh SPARC calls, delay-slot
 restore and DECOMPILE_MODE

- New architecture kArchSparc64_SLEIGH ("sparc64_sleigh"): Ghidra's
  SparcV9_64.sla with a State laid out after its register space
  (SPARC64/Runtime/SleighState.h), a register table, and a
  sparc64_sleigh.bc runtime. Arch::IsSPARC32/IsSPARC64 also accept the
  Sleigh variants.
- SPARC (32 and 64): DECOMPILE_MODE is a decoding-context value of 1, as
  in SparcV9.pspec, so save/restore do not spill the register window
  through computed register-space addresses.
- ControlFlowStructuring: ignore p-code after the first CALL/CALLIND
  (unreachable in the p-code CFG unless an intra-instruction branch
  targets it), so SPARC calls are categorized as calls; and categorize
  instructions that mix intra-instruction branches with exits by their
  exits (e.g. ret with restore in the delay slot).
- SPARC32: the FS/FD/FQ overlays follow Ghidra's big-endian register
  numbering on a little-endian host.
